  Divine gifts always arrive fooproofed (Just don't let a rust
monster chew the rustproofing off of your metal divine gifts. :-)


  Wished for items can be wished for fooproofed.

  A minor point:  With two similar types of armor, both of which
give the same total AC boost, pick the one with the lower base
armor class.  e.g.  a +1 orcish helm over a +0 dwarven helm.
The enchantment is mostly vulnerable to disenchanters.
While the 2 base ac of the dwarven helm can bot be rusted away.
Plus the higher base AC piece of armor tends to be heavier.


  Magical boots (which most players will use for the endgame)
have base armor of 1.  Gloves, helms, small shields ditto.

  That's 4 points of armor class max to be lost.

  Silver shields have base armor of 2, but don't need
fooproofing.

  Cloaks of protection have base AC of 3.  This looks like the
biggest place to get hurt, but few people seem to be big fans of
Cloaks of protection, for the endgame particularly.

  There are some other base 2 shields, again weight vs loseable
AC come into it.

  Swords/shields from angelic beings are always (?) fooproofed,
and can by polymorphed.


  Illiterate conduct almost requires lack of foo-proofing, yet
that doesn't seem to be mentioned as one of the major problems
of illiterate ascensions.


